11. Testing and troubleshooting
Use Apple's StoreKit/sandbox testing and Google Play's licensing and test subscription facilities. Accelerated renewal behavior and simulated failure cases are not identical to real production timing. Test both client UI and backend state transitions.
Symptom	Likely cause	Diagnostic action
Paid user remains Free	Client callback succeeded; server verification missing/failed	Trace verification request, store response, DB commit, grant recomputation
User loses access on cancellation	Cancellation treated as expiration	Check verified paid-through date and revocation state
Duplicate premium grants	Notification handler not idempotent	Inspect event uniqueness and transactional update behavior
Wrong user has Premium	Purchase ownership not enforced	Audit lineage-to-account bindings and restore flow
Renewals never update	RTDN/V2 notifications misconfigured	Verify notification delivery/authentication and run reconciliation
Google purchase refunded unexpectedly	Required acknowledgement not completed	Inspect purchase states and acknowledgement processing
Webhook retry storm	Acknowledgement before durability or persistent 5xx	Inspect queue, delivery logs, backoff and dead-letter policy
Upgrade loses access temporarily	Old/new identifiers treated as unrelated	Examine platform replacement and lineage tracking


Automated test cases: purchase success; pending purchase; invalid signature; wrong bundle/package ID; duplicate transaction; cancellation; grace; hold; refund; expired entitlement; reinstall; account conflict; delayed event; queue outage; store API outage; cross-device synchronization; upgrades/downgrades.

Example application-level test:
// Pseudocode-style Jest test; fakeStore and service are project-owned fixtures.
it("retains access after cancellation until verified expiration", async () => {
  fakeStore.setVerifiedSubscription({
    canceledAutoRenew: true,
    paidThrough: new Date("2026-12-01T00:00:00Z"),
    revoked: false
  });
  await service.reconcile("subscription_1");
  expect(await service.canAccess("user_1", "training_plans", new Date("2026-11-01")))
    .toBe(true);
});
12. Implementation checklist
- [ ] Define plan-to-feature mapping independent of store identifiers.
- [ ] Configure Apple products/groups and Google subscriptions/base plans/offers.
- [ ] Model accounts, transactions, subscription lineage, notification inbox, and grants.
- [ ] Verify app identity, product, signed data/token, lifecycle, and account ownership server-side.
- [ ] Acknowledge eligible Google purchases according to official requirements.
- [ ] Enforce every premium backend action through an entitlement service.
- [ ] Verify notification authenticity; persist and deduplicate before acknowledgement.
- [ ] Fetch current store state during notification processing.
- [ ] Add scheduled reconciliation, retry/backoff, dead-letter queue, and alerts.
- [ ] Support restore purchases and controlled account recovery.
- [ ] Test failures, revocations, renewals, tier changes, and cross-device access.
- [ ] Review privacy, secrets, logs, monitoring, and operational runbooks.
